// S-614 (W5-12 U3b, spec §4.2, §6.4, §13.4): `put_int` in the C of the host, as fixed_str_put_int.onsa says it in the interpreter: every type that satisfies `Int` (`I8 I16 I32 I64 U8 U16 U32 U64`) with 0, 1, MIN, MAX,
// the neighbours of them and the edges of the number of the digits, and for the signed types the negative ones. The longest text, `I64.MIN`, is 20 bytes. The values are the decimal of the number (no leading zeros, `-` first for a negative).
// `case(i)` picks the i-th case by a `match` that is a statement and returns whether the case holds (false for an `i` that is not a case); the sequence of the `[[test.host]]` runs every `i`. A `mode = "test"`
// case runs the interpreter only, and the C is made from the sequence above, so the interpreter and the C give the same bytes for every case here (the C rounds by `onsa_round_f64`).

use std.text.FixedStr

fn int_str[T: Int](v: T) -> FixedStr[24] {
  var t: FixedStr[24] = ""
  t.put_int!(v)
  t
}

// I8 -128
fn c0() -> Bool {
  int_str(I8.MIN) == "-128"
}

